Description:

backupcyrusd now works with directory-based cyrusdb backends such as zeroskip.
Message annotations are fetched per message with the new FANNOT command, which
replaces the raw per-mailbox annotations database.  The seen and subscription
databases are sent as JSON objects of their keys and values, whatever their
backend.


Documentation:

The protocol is described in comments in imap/backupcyrusd.c.


Config changes:

None.


Upgrade instructions:

Upgrade backupcyrusd and the Cyrus::Backup client together.  The backup state
version is now 7; older states gain the new indexed.modseq column on their next
backup.  That backup fetches annotations for every message and replaces the
seen and sub files with their JSON form.  Backups taken before this change keep
a raw cyrus.annotations file for each folder, and the client removes it the
next time the folder changes.


GitHub issue:

None.
